    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76184" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄχαν-ον</span></b> , τό,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔχω</span> A) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>holder of a shield</i>, i.e. <i>a bar</i> or
				<i>band fastened crosswise on the under side of the
			shield</i>, through which the bearer passed his arm, <i><span class="en">
				Anacr.
				91
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.141
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aen.Tact.
				29.12
			</span></i>; invented by the Carians acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.171
			</span></i>.</div>
